   244	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   245	    """
   246	    Reassemble scattered multicolor strip-fragments into a left-right symmetric rectangle by combining edge-color matching with quarter-turn recovery.
   247	
   248	    Input structure:
   249	    - The background is the dominant color.
   250	    - One multicolor component already sits in output position: its majority color forms a 5-column rectangular border, and two minority pixels inside that border mark the top and bottom chain anchors.
   251	    - Every other non-background component is a 3x3 patch whose majority color is a 1x3 body strip; two minority pixels encode the strip's edge colors, and the whole patch may be rotated by 0/90/180/270 degrees.
   252	
   253	    Rule:
   254	    - Treat each non-background connected component as one piece, using its majority color as the body and the two minority pixels as edge hints.
   255	    - The frame fixes the output size. For every scattered 3x3 piece, try all quarter-turns and keep the rotations that convert it back into a horizontal strip with one hint above and one hint below.
   256	    - Starting from the frame's top anchor color, choose an unused strip orientation whose upper hint matches the current required color, place its body on the next interior row, then continue with that strip's lower hint until the bottom frame anchor is reached.
